== Hizerbruch
 Classify compactification of $CC^(n)$ $(X,B)$ such that $ X without B tilde.equiv CC^(n) $ such that $ b_(2)(X)= 1 $

  + $ n = 1,2,(bb(P)^(n),bb(P)^(n - 1)) $
  +  for $ n gt.eq.slant 3 $, $(bb(P)^(n),bb(P)^(n - 1)),(Q_(n) subset bb(P)^(n + 1),Q_(n) sect H) $
  + $ n = 3 $ if $D $ smooth (called smooth compactification), $X $ not fano, then $(bb(P)^(3),bb(P)^(2)) $
  +  true for Kahler assumption.

    -  proved for $ n <= 6 $ by Fujita
    -  short proof for $ n 3 mod 4 $ by Li-Peternell
    -  implied by $ D tilde.equiv bb(P)^(n - 1) $ and $ <-> c_(1)(D)= n $

